[{"id":3520721097,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7R2fDJ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The fix makes sense to me.\r\n\r\nWhat I don't understand is why the remap cache isn't _always_ local. Duplication is a tree operation, so why isn't the duplication tracking map initialized and destructed in the top node (RAII style), but instead some operation in the tree is allocating it on the stack on demand?\r\nSince this is an important fix, I'm fine with merging this change as-is, but I think this setup needs further review in the future.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113179#pullrequestreview-3520721097","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113179","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113179#pullrequestreview-3520721097"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113179"}},"submitted_at":"2025-11-29T14:34:37Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3521809973,"node_id"